# Scanner false-positive / inconclusive-review ledgers (agent-manager-hygiene's
# suppression-store.js). When pipelineDir == repoRoot (the self-hosting pipeline) these
# land at repo root, where git-runner.js's `git stash push -u` before every resetToMain()
# was sweeping them into an abandoned stash -- 13 correctly-recorded false-positive
# suppressions lost that way over 3 days, so the scanner kept re-flagging the same
# constructs forever. Ignoring them keeps `stash -u` off them (it skips ignored files).
scanner-suppressions.json
scanner-review-attempts.json
dashboard.pid
.claude/
brain-dump.json
concepts.json
project-history.json
projects.json
runs/
.agent-manager-discuss-sessions.json
.agent-manager-chat-sessions.json
dashboard-settings.json
vendor/tokenfold/core/build/
# Runtime log reclaim-orphaned-drafts.js appends to at pipelineDir root (2026-09-15,
# found live during a GitHub-vs-local sync check) -- same class of leak
# pipeline-state-gitignored.test.js's invariant exists to catch generally, missed here
# since this path is a hardcoded literal in reclaim-orphaned-drafts.js, not exposed via
# getConfig() the way that test's own coverage walks.
reclaim-log.jsonl
# task-logs/<id>.json (src/task-log-store.js) was previously deliberately git-tracked and
# committed alongside every applied task's real change, as a durable snapshot surviving
# queue/ archival -- see that module's own header. RE-EVALUATED 2026-09-15, Grimmethy:
# this repo is PUBLIC on GitHub, and task-logs/ retains a task's full promptContext.rawText
# / implementResponse / planResponse verbatim -- for a brain_dump-derived task that is the
# user's own free-typed personal/business note text (confirmed live: 13 of 48 already-
# committed task-logs/ entries originate from brain-dump entries, the same free-text
# source a captured note with a private Google Sheets link was sitting in). No amount of
# redacting individual fields is as safe as simply not tracking this directory at all --
# still written locally (apply-task.js/task-log-store.js unchanged otherwise) for the
# user's own reference, just never staged/committed/pushed.
task-logs/
